BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-AM64x-PD23.2.0               2023-09-29
==========================================================

- Linux TI vendor kernel v6.1.33 (based on TI tag 09.00.00.007)
- U-Boot TI vendor v2023.04 (based on TI tag 09.00.00.007)
- Yocto 4.0.12 (kirkstone)


Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------

- phytec-headless-image:
  * phyboard-electra-am64xx-1
  * phyboard-electra-am64xx-2


Build Environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 20.04 64-bit


Change Log:
-----------

- UART boot source is now available
- Inline ECC is enabled by default
- EEPROM SOM detection for Ethernet PHY, SPI-NOR Flash, and RTC populated options
- Watchdog support
- GPIO FAN with pre-set thermal zone
- TSN support for Ethernet
- Virtualization with Podman/Docker


Issues Fixed:
-------------

- ADC channels are configured correctly
- USB support in U-Boot


 Known Issues:
-------------

- The flashcp command occasionally fails during the verification step.
- The reboot command delays the reboot process by several seconds in 5% of all boots.
- USB devices connected to the USB bus on the PCIe connector might not be detected during boot or can fail during operation in some cases.
- The PCIe card with an I210 was not detected in 5% of all boots.
